    "mistake.006.situation" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Code like if (retryCount > 3), setTimeout(() => {}, 86400000), and if (role === 2) is scattered everywhere. Only the author knows what the 3, the 86400000, and the 2 mean. When the policy changes and the retry count has to become 5, you have to find every 3 in the codebase, and since other 3s mean other things, you risk changing the wrong one."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "if (retryCount > 3), setTimeout(() => {}, 86400000), if (role === 2) 같은 코드가 여기저기 흩어져 있습니다. 3이 뭐고, 86400000은 뭐고, 2가 뭔지 작성자만 알고 있습니다. 정책이 바뀌어 재시도 횟수를 5로 늘려야 할 때, 코드 전체에서 3을 찾아야 하는데 다른 의미의 3도 있어 잘못 수정할 위험이 있습니다."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.007.action" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Follow your team's coding conventions, and set up automation like ESLint, Prettier, or SwiftLint in your project. If you set up format-on-save, you won't even have to think about style. If there are no conventions yet, propose some to your team and use an industry standard (such as the Airbnb Style Guide) as a starting point."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "팀이 정한 코딩 컨벤션을 따르고, ESLint, Prettier, SwiftLint 같은 자동화 도구를 프로젝트에 설정하세요. 저장 시 자동 포맷팅을 설정하면 스타일에 대해 생각할 필요조차 없어집니다. 컨벤션이 없다면 팀에 제안하고, 업계 표준(Airbnb Style Guide 등)을 출발점으로 삼으세요."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "mistake.007.growth" : {
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "You learn the teamwork principle that consistency matters more than personal taste. You also learn the efficiency of not spending human energy on things a tool can automate. This directly affects team productivity and how quickly new people get up to speed."
          }
        },
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
