        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "To find a bug, you sprinkle console.log('here1'), console.log('here2'), and console.log(data) all over your code. In complex logic you end up with dozens of print statements, and cleaning them up afterward is a chore. In asynchronous code the output order gets scrambled, which makes things even more confusing."
